A||||6||JohnnyK||Anyone familiar with pool heaters?||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||06-18-2001||06:40 PM||||It's a "teledyne series One" or soemthing likle that. Big natural gas heater. BUT, the problem has arrived again, we open the pool, and the damn heater doesn't work. The pilot light is burning, so thats not the problem.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> the pool is at 70 now, and I crank the temp control to max, which SHOULD fire the heater up, but it does nothing. i seem to remember a thermostat or somethjing going out last time.. could just be my imagination though. That happen alot?||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||06-18-2001||08:18 PM||||I don't know how the thermostat is built for that. would not suprise me if it's shot. Pool stuff does that. How many wires go to the thermostat.<P>As for fixing it... hard to say. being a gas heater I'm not going to guess. Screwing up that thing could take a whole block out.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||06-18-2001||10:24 PM||||Also your thermocouple could be shot(that's the devise that opens the gas valve only if the pilot is burning) It looks like a piece of wire that sticks into the flame of the pilot light.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Robert||06-18-2001||10:29 PM||||Sounds like the same problem I had with my hot tub.  The repairperson jumped the wires on the thermocouple and the heater fired up.  After that it worked fine on it’s own.  He said I my need to replace it sometime in the future, but it seems to be working now. <BR>Robert<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||06-19-2001||01:03 AM||||Lately, my pool has been at 86 degrees, just heated by the sun.  We just take the solar cover off when it's going to be a hot day and then put it back on at night if it's going to be cool.  The only sort of heating apparatus that we were thinking of getting is a solar collector panel.<P>As for the thermocouple, those typically go bad on furnaces and (house)water heaters, so I wouldnt be surprised if yours is bad either.  It also very well may be a typical type, and not some special order part, so you might be able to find one at your local hardware.  We carry 4 different lengths at mine and they run about $3.99<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000005||JohnnyK||06-19-2001||02:39 AM||||Well, I can only assume that the piece I am looking at is the thermostat. Has a thin piece of tubing running DIRECTLY into it (stops right there) and I loosened it, and water started shooting out (the thing that bothers me though, is if it was the thermostat, shouldn't it be running through it, instead of just into it and stopping?). There are two wires going to it. I touched them together, and nothing happened?||||reg||1
Z||000006||JohnnyK||06-19-2001||06:37 PM||||Teledyne-Laars actually.. I found a metal coated wire going down to the pilot. I thought it might have been a piezo spark or something, but then I realized you have to light it with a match. The wire comes up and there are two wires coming out of the tube, which are connected to the thing (with the switch for lighting the pilot, etc) I took a paperclip and connected the two screws that the wires clip onto.. Nothing.. I also tried connecting the two prongs on what I believe is the thermostat.  Anythign I'm missing? There doesn't seem to be any power going into the thing (no electrical cords or anything)||||reg||1
